Our research addresses the limitations of existing caching strategies in IoT by introducing a holistic framework that integrates real-time monitoring and adaptive prioritization based on CF and PoA. While prior methods such as m-CAC, m-Greedy, and m-Myopic have been used as benchmarks, each focuses on a single caching parameter—popularity, frequency, or recency, respectively—and lacks adaptability to the multi-dimensional and dynamic nature of context in IoT systems~\cite{Muller2017}. In contrast, our proposed DCMF framework leverages MAUT and DST to enable decision-making, ensuring that only the most relevant and timely context is cached. This results in reduced latency, minimized expiry, and improved responsiveness, establishing DCMF as a comprehensive and state-of-the-art approach for context caching.


