The DCMF's CAPME dynamically calculates PoA by analyzing query patterns in real time. Using these query rates, the utility scores in the MAUT framework were adjusted to prioritize high-PoA CIs. For instance, CIs with query counts exceeding 1,000 during peak hours were assigned a significantly higher utility score compared to items accessed less frequently. This adjustment ensured that frequently queried items remained cached.

