\section{Introduction}\label{sec1}
Anderson extrapolation \cite{anderson1965iterative, anderson2019comments,ouyang2020anderson,toth2015,zhu2022integral,fung2022jfb} has recently been applied to deep equilibrium models (DEQs) \cite{bai2022equilibrium, bai2019deep,bai2020multiscale,bai2021stabilizing,huang2021textrm,geng2021training}. Kolter et al. \cite{kolter2020} found the gains not substantial due to early termination with a loose convergence tolerance. They focused on Anderson extrapolation during training. Here, we show significant acceleration of AI performance with Anderson on GPUs for both the forward pass (running inferences faster) and training (generating models faster). We demonstrate acceleration of the forward pass with standard Anderson as a baseline for future work with stochastic variants \cite{wei2021stochastic} and accelerating the backward pass with Jacobian-free methods like Jacobian-Free Backpropagation (JFB) and Neumann series gradient approximations \cite{fung2022jfb}.

