To illustrate the effectiveness of the proposed PED loss, we present two simple toy networks, as shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:case}\textbf{(a)}. Both networks, $G^{(1)}$ and $G^{(2)}$, have the same set of nodes but differ in their connectivity patterns. Specifically, $G^{(2)}$ includes two additional edges---(2, 6) and (3, 5)---compared to $G^{(1)}$.
