\begin{proof}
$(\Rightarrow)$ Suppose $\varphi$ is definable by an $\LS$-formula $\varphi'$ and $\sigma=\sig(\varphi)\cup \sig(\varphi')$. By definition, $\sigma$ contains no constants. Take any pointed $\sigma$-structure $\Amf,a$. By the choice of $\varphi'$ and Lemmas~\ref{lemma:bisim_omega} and~\ref{lemma:equivalenceomega}, $\Amf\models \varphi(a)$ iff $\Amf\models \varphi'(a)$ iff $\Amf^\omega \models \varphi'(a,0)$ iff $\Amf^\omega \models \varphi(a,0)$ iff $\Amf^\omega \models \Flat(\varphi)(a,0)$ iff $\Amf \models \Flat(\varphi)(a)$, which yields  $\models \varphi\leftrightarrow \Flat(\varphi)$. The implication $(\Leftarrow)$ is trivial.
\end{proof}

