We show by induction that, for any $\chi\in\sub(\varphi_1,\varphi_2)$ and any $s$ of the form \eqref{eq1second}, we have $\Amf_{i}\models \chi(s)$ iff $\chi\in \type_{n}$. The basis of induction and the Boolean cases of the induction step are trivial. Suppose $\Amf_{i}\models \Du\chi(s)$. Then $\Amf_{i}\models \chi(s')$, for some $s' \in \dom(\Amf_{i})$. It $\type'$ is the type of $s'$, then $\chi \in \type'$ by IH, and so $\Du \chi \in \type'$ and $\Du \chi \in \type_n$. 
