\in \type_n$, we need to prove that $P_{S}(\frak{s}_{p},\frak{s}_{c})$ contains $\Diamond_S^{> \mx}\chi$ or $\Diamond_S^{= m}\chi$, for some $m \ge k$, which follows from IH and conditions {\bf (witness$_1$)} and {\bf (witness$_2$)}. The converse implication also follows from {\bf (witness$_1$)}, {\bf (witness$_2$)} and IH.

