with $n\geq 0$, $j\in \{0,1\}$, $a_{i}\in \dom(\Amf)$ for all $i\leq n$, and $S_{i}$ either a binary predicate symbol in $\sig(\varphi)$ or its inverse, and such that $(a_{i},a_{i+1})\in S_{i}^{\Amf}$ for $i\leq n$. For $\vec{a}$ of the form \eqref{eq:def1}, let $\text{tail}(\vec{a})=a_{n}^{j}$. Set $\vec{a}\in A^{\Amf^{\ast}}$ if $a_{n}\in A^{\Amf}$ for 
