    $(\implies)$ Assuming $\TWelfare$ has a dictator at $i$, and considering an arbitrary $p \in \PN$, we prove $\TWelfare(p) \veebar p_i = p_i$ as follows: Firstly, if $p_i = \i$, then $\TWelfare(p) \veebar p_i = \TWelfare(p) \veebar \i = \i = p_i$ is satisfied for all possible values of $\TWelfare(p) \in \TPrefs$. Otherwise, if $p_i \neq \i$ then Condition (1) implies $\TWelfare(p) \neq \c$, which implies $\TWelfare(p) \veebar p_i = \TWelfare(p) \vee p_i$. But Condition (2) of Definition \ref{definition:dictator-generalised} implies $\TWelfare(p) \leq p_i$, which implies $p_i = \TWelfare(p) \vee p_i$. Combining the two facts, $\TWelfare(p) \veebar p_i = \TWelfare(p) \vee p_i = p_i$ as desired.\\

