    In $\L_0$, complements satisfy $\forall X \in \L_0$: $X \wedge \neg X = \bot$ and $X \vee \neg X = \top$. We have that $A = A \wedge \neg B$ by the following derivation:
    \begin{align*}
        A\  & =\quad  A \wedge \top                       &  & \text{$\top$ is the top of $\L_0$}            \\
            & =\quad  A \wedge (B \vee \neg B)            &  & \text{$B \vee \neg B = \top$}                 \\
            & =\quad  (A \wedge B) \vee (A \wedge \neg B) &  & \text{Distributivity of $\wedge$ over $\vee$} \\
