\section{Formal Problem and Preliminaries}\label{sec:prelims}

We formalize the ``text summarization'' problem by describing the (i) {\em input} to the problem, 
(ii) desired {\em output}, and (iii) approaches that we use for measuring \emph{utility}.

\paragraph{Input.}
The input is a dataset of conversations $\bx=\{x_1,\ldots,x_n\}$, where each element $x_i$ represents a conversation between a user and an LLM.

\paragraph{Output.}
The desired output for our problem is $\bs = \{s_1, s_2, \ldots, s_m\} \in \cS^*$ consisting of \emph{summaries} $s_j \in \cS$. The set $\cS$ is potentially infinite (e.g., the set of all strings in our case).
The DP guarantee applies only to this output set s of summaries.
