\subsection{Post-PBS Analysis of MEV Builders} \label{sec_appendix_postpbs}

As explained in Section~\ref{sec_appendix_mev}, proposer-builder separation (PBS) was designed to create a competitive marketplace for block builders to ameliorate the negative externalities of maximal extractable value (MEV). Here, we report data on the MEV builders involved after the implementation of MEV-Boost, which is coincident on the same day as the Ethereum Merge. Figure~\ref{fig_mev_blocks} shows the daily fraction of blocks that have used MEV (left) and the daily fraction of proposers (\textit{i.e.}, validators) that have produced at least one MEV block.

