\section{Experimental Setup}\label{sec4:experimentation}

In this section, we detail the experiments conducted to evaluate the three different approaches.

\subsection{Max-Cut Benchmark Description} \label{subsec:MaxCutBenchmark}
The experiments are carried out on a variety of graph instances of the Weighted Max-Cut problem (see Section \ref{subsec:MAXCUT}). Specifically, we evaluate each solver using a benchmark of 15 instances provided in \cite{eneko}. This selection enables a rigorous and meaningful comparison by leveraging a dataset with established reference results. The benchmark comprises 15 weighted graph instances of varying sizes, ranging from $N=10$ nodes to $N=250$ nodes, with edge weights uniformly distributed in the range $[0, 2]$. Table \ref{tab:maxcut_bench} summarizes a detailed description of all benchmark instances.

