Since both the objective function \eqref{const-hjb1} and the safety constraint \eqref{const-hjb2} are convex with respect to $u_i$, the optimal solution can be characterized using the KKT conditions. Specifically, for agent $i$, the safe optimal controller $u_{i}^*$ and the optimal value function $V_{i}^*(e_i)$ are obtained as 
% Since the objective function (\ref{const-hjb1}) and the safety constraint (\ref{const-hjb2}) are convex with respect to $u_i$, for each agent $i\in V_a$, the safe optimal controller $u_{i}^*$ and the optimal value function $V_{i}^*$ can be obtained by following the KKT conditions
\begin{subequations}\label{kkt}
\begin{align}
