\begin{remark}
Our method provides an HJB-based centralized training framework and a distributed deployment paradigm using GNNs. It eliminates the need for global information aggregation during deployment, as required in~\cite{Safaoui2024tro}, thereby enhancing scalability and practicality in large-scale MAS with limited sensing radius. Notably, the framework involves training with only a small number of agents (e.g., 8 in all our trainings. See Section~\ref{Section5}). It generalizes effectively to much larger MAS with hundreds or even thousands of agents.
\end{remark}



\subsection{Design of Loss Functions}\label{Section4.2}
In this section, to jointly train the value function $V_\theta(e_i)$, the graph CBF $h_{\omega}(\eta_i)$, and the distributed safe controller $\pi_{\varphi}(\eta_i)$, we 
% For the multi-agent systems (\ref{mas}), to jointly train the value function $V_\theta$, the GCBF $h_{\omega}$, and the distributed controller $\pi_{\varphi}$, we 
propose to minimize the following total loss function $L(\theta,\omega,\varphi)$, which is composed of three components: the value function loss $L_{v}(\theta,\varphi)$, the graph CBF loss $L_h(\omega,\varphi)$, and the distributed safe controller loss $L_\pi(\theta,\omega,\varphi)$: 
\begin{align}\label{L}
L(\theta,\omega,\varphi)=L_{v}(\theta,\varphi)+L_h(\omega,\varphi)+L_\pi(\theta,\omega,\varphi), 
\end{align}
where $L_{*}=\sum_{i\in V_a}L_{*i}$, and $*$ takes $v,h,\pi.$
% \begin{subequations}\label{Li}
% \begin{align}
% L_{v}(\theta,\varphi)=&\sum_{i\in V_a}L_{vi}(\theta,\varphi),\\
% L_h(\omega,\varphi)=&\sum_{i\in V_a}L_{hi}(\omega,\varphi),\\
% L_\pi(\theta,\omega,\varphi)=&\sum_{i\in V_a}L_{\pi i}(\theta,\omega,\varphi),
% \end{align}    
