We construct two datasets, $D_i^C$ and $D_i^A$ inspired by \cite{zhang2025tro}, which consist of input features labeled as safe and unsafe, respectively. The graph CBF loss $L_{hi}(\omega,\varphi)$ of agent $i$ encourages the satisfaction of safety constraint (\ref{CBF_N_R}) and the safety requirement from $H_{N,i} \subseteq S_i$, $i\in V_a$ in Theorem~\ref{the1}, i.e., 
\begin{align}\label{lhi}
&L_{hi}(\omega,\varphi)\nonumber\\
=&\sum_{\eta_i\in D_{i}^C}\max\big\{0,\varsigma-h_{\omega}(\eta_i)\big\}+\sum_{\eta_i\in D_{i}^A}\max\big\{0,\varsigma+h_{\omega}(\eta_i)\big\}\nonumber\\
&+b_h\sum_{\eta_i}\max\big\{0,\varsigma-\dot{h}_{\omega}(\eta_i)-\alpha(h_{\omega}(\eta_i))\big\},
\end{align}
where $\varsigma>0$ is a weight that encourages these inequalities on system safety to strictly be satisfied, and $b_h>0$ is a constant weight. 

