Moreover, the controller loss function $L_{\pi i}(\theta,\omega,\varphi)$ minimizes the deviation between the learned distributed controller $\pi_\varphi(\eta_i)$ and the approximated KKT-based safe controller $\hat{u}_{i}$ instead of QP-CBF controller used in \cite{zhang2025tro}:
\begin{align}\label{lui}
L_{\pi i}(\theta,\omega,\varphi)=b_{\pi}\|\pi_{\varphi}(\eta_i)-\hat{u}_{i}\|,
\end{align}
with $b_{\pi}>0$ a constant weight and 
\begin{align}\label{appro-us}
\hat{u}_{i}=-\frac{1}{2}R^{-1}g^T(x_i)\Big(\nabla_{e_i}  V_\theta(e_i)-\hat{\lambda}_i\nabla_{\eta_i} h_{\omega}(\eta_i)\Big),
\end{align}
where $\hat{\lambda}_i$ is approximated Lagrange multiplier satisfying 
\begin{align}\label{appro-lag}
\hat{\lambda}_i=\begin{cases}
-\frac{\hat{\Lambda}_h}{\hat{\vartheta}_h},& {\rm if}\ \hat{\Lambda}_h<0,\\
0,& {\rm if}\ \hat{\Lambda}_h\ge0,
\end{cases}
\end{align} 
with $\hat{\Lambda}_h$, $\hat{\vartheta}_h$ denoting approximations of \eqref{lagrange2}, \eqref{lagrange3} when replacing $V_i^*(e_i)$ and $h(\bar{x}_{N_i})$ with simultaneously updated $V_\theta(e_i)$ and $h_{\omega}(\eta_i)$, respectively. Specifically, $\hat{u}_i$ characterizes an analytically structured approximation of optimal control, balancing goal-reaching and safety via the approximated Lagrange multiplier $\hat{\lambda}_i$. By minimizing the deviation between $\pi_\varphi(\eta_i)$ and $\hat{u}_{i}$, the controller loss (\ref{lui}) guides the learned controller to inherit the safety guarantees, goal-reaching performance, and optimality structure encoded in the HJB-KKT formulation. 
% This not only improves the interpretability and theoretical grounding of the learned policy but also facilitates distributed safe policy learning within the HJB-GNN framework. 
Overall, the training is performed by minimizing (\ref{L}) via gradient descent, during which all three neural network parameters $\theta$, $\omega$, and $\varphi$ are updated simultaneously.


