% \iffalse\BGI{The introduction about PBDS needs to be expanded. Essentially, the reader needs to be provided with enough background to understand the problem we are solving}\fi
% we developed provenance-based data skipping (PBDS) before, a novel approach that generates provenance sketches which are concise encodings of what data is relevant for a query. Provenance sketch consists of several partitions containing the provenance which is relevant for answering the query. Given a horizontal partition of an input table, the provenance sketch records the fragments of partition containing the provenance. Thus, first step to implement the provenance sketch is create a horizontal partitions, typically the range partitioning of input data which is based on the range of attributes of the tables. If we evaluate a query over its provenance this yields the same result as evaluating the query over the full database, we claim that this provenance sketch is safe. We developed safety rules which analyze statically the input query and tables to determine which attributes of the tables are safe to capture provenance sketch on. Thus, the candidates of attributes for creating horizontal partitions can be generated by safety rules. Once a provenance sketch has been captured it is used to speed up subsequent queries.

