To do so, we spawn exactly 84 thread blocks (number of SMs) to ensure even GPU utilization, and vary the amount of threads per block. Given the number of threads per block \smalltt{NBTHREAD} and the number of blocks \smalltt{NBLOCK} (=84), this makes
thread~\smalltt{TID} responsible for processing the lookups at positions \smalltt{TID + i * NBTHREAD * NBLOCK}. This essentially replaces the GPU's dynamic thread scheduler with a static assignment between tasks and cores.

