\subsection{Scaling Binary and $K$-ary Search}
\vspace*{-0.1cm}

Finally, we compare the scaling behavior by re-running the experiment from Figure~\ref{fig:rx:scaling} to compare the lookup time of \ks{} against our best-performing binary search variant from the previous sections, as well as the baseline indexes.
The results are shown in Figure~\ref{fig:exp:ks_scaling}.
Also, as \ks{} introduces time and space overhead over \bs{} during the build process when materializing the separators in main memory, we compare their respective memory footprints in Figure~\ref{fig:exp:memory_footprint}, and build times in Figure~\ref{fig:exp:build_time}.

